{"created": "2026-04-17T11:02:55.596281+00:00", "modified": "2026-04-17T11:02:56.293871+00:00", "id": 19629778, "conceptrecid": "17533199", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19629778", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.17533199", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19629778", "metadata": {"title": "Supplementary Dataset for \"Dynamic 3D MRI of vocal fold oscillations: In vivo assessment of vocal fold thickness, contact area, and glottal area waveform across phonation types in comparison with high-speed imaging\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19629778", "publication_date": "2026", "description": "<p>This Zenodo record contains the supplementary dataset for the manuscript <em>&ldquo;Dynamic 3D MRI of vocal fold oscillations: In vivo assessment of vocal fold thickness, contact area, and glottal area waveform across phonation types in comparison with high-speed imaging&rdquo;</em> (submitted to the <em>Journal of the Acoustical Society of America</em>).</p>\n<p>The dataset includes:<br>&bull; 60 dynamic 3D MRI volumes (.nrrd)<br>&bull; 60 surface reconstructions (.stl)<br>&bull; 12 synchronized audio recordings (.wav)<br>&bull; supplementary video animations (.mp4): <span>HSV recordings with simultaneous EGG and GAW presentation (supplement video S1_HSV_EGG_GAW.mp4), </span><span>animation of 3D surface reconstruction in 6 phonation types (supplement video S2: dynamic 3D surface reconstruction.mp4), </span><span>Animation of sagittal, coronal, and axial views of 3D dynamic vocal fold MRI for six phonation types (supplement video S3_slices animation.gif), </span><span>Dynamic VF contact area animation in saggital slice for 6 phonation types (supplement video S4_contact area.gif)</span></p>\n<p>All files retain their original folder structure in ZIP archives. The dataset will be made publicly available upon article acceptance under a CC BY 4.0 license.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Traser, Louisa", "affiliation": "Freiburger Institut f\u00fcr Musikermedizin", "o